  greetings:
  - Coffee? It's on the house if you don't tell Mama.
  - You're the detective. Lyle won't shut up about you.
  aboutSelf: I waitress for Mama. I was in Tulsa four years, then Daddy died and I came home, and I don't really remember deciding to stay.
  aboutTown: Everybody here's lived through something that left a mark. We don't stare at each other's marks. It's polite.
  seenAnythingStrange: Somebody's been sitting in the back booth after close. The seat's still warm in the morning, and there's a full cup of coffee gone stone cold. Nobody drank it.
  foundersDay: Rained. Mama won, cherry. I helped with the crust and she won't admit it.
  gossip:
  - title: About Doc Abner Pruitt
    response: Doc's left eye is glass. He takes it out to scare the kids. It worked on me till I was twenty.
  - title: About Bev Thorne
    response: Bev lost her left hand to a thresher. Wears a hook. She can open a bottle with it faster than Silas can with an opener.
